From 923a72e267dba52a292f0f204d42c47159b10c87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 21:24:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 275/275] fix(avx512): declare the AVX2 prerequisite of the
 native position plane

- -mavx512f implicitly enables AVX2 and the compare/where kernels execute 16
  VEX.256 instructions from the auto-vectorized reduction tails; the
  declaration and runtime gate now name avx2 (required_features) and the
  native feature mask gains bit 0x80 (default variant 0x01 -> 0x81)
- probe AVX2 independently from CPUID.(EAX=7,ECX=0):EBX[5] with OS YMM state;
  a host feature set without avx2 fails closed before dlopen
- bump artifact payload 8 -> 9 (prerequisite semantics change); the ABI marker
  stays :9 because no symbol/calling contract changed (an old runtime still
  rejects the new native_feature_mask, a new runtime rejects payload 8)
- compile flags unchanged (no -mno-avx2); numerical outputs are byte-identical
- tests: required_features/mask assertions, missing-avx2 rejection test and
  updated payload assertions

(cherry picked from commit 3e378ecffcf4d8d504c4518992ea71d5974db1b7)
